            <ul>
                <li><strong>Rapid Proof-of-Concept (POC) Delivery:</strong> Compressed enterprise solution vision and high-fidelity POC turnaround from <strong>2 months to 2 weeks</strong> using generative AI workflows and interactive prototypes, accelerating pre-sales alignment and executive stakeholder buy-in.</li>
                <li><strong>Government Solutions Architecture (ProcureSight):</strong> Architected enterprise solution workflows for <strong>ProcureSight</strong>, Appian’s flagship government acquisition offering used widely across federal agencies; leading the transition from semantic search to <strong>generative AI-driven vendor insights and recommendations</strong>.</li>
                <li><strong>Enterprise Value &amp; Client Enablement:</strong> Partnered with client-facing teams and commercial stakeholders across <strong>92 enterprise customer accounts</strong> (e.g., Porsche, Pfizer, T. Rowe Price), achieving a <strong>60% usability improvement</strong> and standardizing accessibility across platforms.</li>
                <li><strong>Implementation Efficiency &amp; Frameworks:</strong> Designed foundational platform frameworks (Rules Engine, Workflow system, Solutions Hub) that saved client implementation teams <strong>2–3 sprints of development</strong> per deployment, enabling partners like DTCC to achieve record delivery velocity.</li>
                <li><strong>Technical Demos &amp; Custom Tooling:</strong> Engineered custom interactive utilities—including <strong>plug-and-play usability testing overlays</strong> and automated audit tools—accelerating client feedback turnaround by <strong>75%</strong> and standardizing team demo infrastructure.</li>
                <li><strong>Full-Stack Technical Feasibility:</strong> Directly authored, tested, and <strong>merged frontend code</strong> (React/JS/SAIL) to demonstrate technical feasibility, bridging the gap between solution architecture and production engineering to ensure <strong>100% fidelity</strong>.</li>
                <li><strong>Executive Briefings &amp; Discovery:</strong> Led interactive discovery tracks and technical solution demonstrations at Appian World across <strong>50+ enterprise client sessions</strong>, translating complex business requirements into clear, value-driven technical architectures.</li>
                <li><strong>Ecosystem &amp; Partner Enablement:</strong> Scaled the external <strong>Figma SAIL Component Library</strong> to <strong>over 1,300 external developers and partners</strong>, standardizing UI architecture for partner consultancies and facilitating cross-department knowledge sessions across 35+ workshops.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="job-item">
            <div class="job-header">
                <div><span class="job-title">FE&nbsp;UI&nbsp;and&nbsp;UX&nbsp;Design&nbsp;Intern</span> | <span class="company">Virsec Systems</span></div>
                <div class="location-date">June 2021 – August 2021</div>
            </div>
            <ul>
                <li>Designed <strong>dashboards and admin utilities</strong> for a cybersecurity platform, partnering with Product Owners to demonstrate CVE threat insights and remediation workflows through <strong>iterative UI prototypes</strong>.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>Education</h2>
        
        <div class="edu-item">
            <div class="edu-header">
                <span class="degree">Master of Business Administration (MBA)</span>
                <span class="location-date">Expected 2028</span>
            </div>
            <div class="school">University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill</div>
        </div>

        <div class="edu-item">
            <div class="edu-header">
                <span class="degree">Master of Science in Information Science</span>
                <span class="location-date">May 2022</span>
            </div>
            <div class="school">University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill</div>
            <div class="edu-details">
                <strong>Specialization:</strong> Human-Computer Interaction Design<br>
                <strong>Research:</strong> Master's Paper: <a href="https://cdr.lib.unc.edu/concern/masters_papers/2r36v751z?locale=en" target="_blank" style="color: var(--color-text); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid #e5e7eb;"><em>User Preferences for Email Tasks on Different Platforms</em></a>. A mixed-methods study analyzing mental models to determine task optimization strategies.
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="edu-item">
            <div class="edu-header">
                <span class="degree">Bachelor of Arts in Philosophy</span>
                <span class="location-date">May 2020</span>
            </div>
            <div class="school">Virginia Tech</div>
            <div class="edu-details">
                <strong>Minors:</strong> Japanese Studies, Creative Writing<br>
                <em>Summa Cum Laude, Honors Laureate</em>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>Skills & Certifications</h2>
        <div class="skill-group">
            <span class="skill-label">Solutions Consulting &amp; Strategy:</span> Pre-Sales Demonstrations, Rapid Proof-of-Concept (POC) Development, Client Discovery, Enterprise Solution Architecture, Business Value &amp; ROI Modeling, Agile/Scrum.
        </div>
        <div class="skill-group">
            <span class="skill-label">Technical &amp; Prototyping:</span> React, JavaScript, HTML/CSS, Git, Figma, AI-Assisted Prototyping (Gemini, Kiro), Appian SAIL (Low-Code), Adobe Creative Cloud.
        </div>
        <div class="skill-group">
            <span class="skill-label">Research &amp; Certifications:</span> Usability Testing, Heuristic Evaluation, Information Architecture, WCAG 2.1 AA Accessibility, Shift Nudge Interface Design (2023), Google UX (2021), CITI Research Ethics (2021).
        </div>
    </section>

    <section style="margin-bottom: 0;">
        <h2>Activities</h2>
        <div class="skill-group">
            <strong>WHEELS Global Foundation</strong> (2025–Present) • <strong>Waffler’s Writing Workshop</strong> (2021–Present, 3 Published Annual Anthologies) • <strong>Eagle Scout</strong> (2016)
        </div>
    </section>
</div>

</body>
</html>
